From: DotRedstone <dotredstone@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: fall back to RDO current without PDO details

The Qualcomm PMIC UCSI implementation used by Xiaomi Sheng reports the
active RDO but does not advertise UCSI_CAP_PDO_DETAILS.  The UCSI power
supply consequently reports current_now correctly while current_max is
always zero.

Use the maximum current requested in the active RDO when source PDOs are
not available.  This keeps the power-supply view useful without
inventing capabilities beyond the negotiated contract.

---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/psy.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/psy.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/psy.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/psy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/psy.c
@@ -158,6 +158,9 @@ static int ucsi_psy_get_current_max(struct ucsi_connector *con,
 			max_current = (pdo_current > max_current) ? pdo_current
 								  : max_current;
 		}
+		if (!max_current && con->rdo)
+			max_current = rdo_max_current(con->rdo) * 1000;
+
 		val->intval = max_current;
 		break;
 	case UCSI_CONSTAT_PWR_OPMODE_TYPEC1_5:
--
2.50.1
